user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 17,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_asserts_propositional_falsity",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment (OC_comments): asserts that the OP's claim or a premise is factually or logically false (1) vs not (0)",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title and argument for the OP's view, then every comment in the OC_comments JSON list (ignore order; do not use conversation). Return 1 if at least one comment asserts that the OP's claim or a stated premise is false, incorrect, or logically invalid as a proposition (e.g. disputing facts, definitions or inference), as opposed to presenting harms. A comment may satisfy both this and the harm-quantification feature. Return 0 if comments are parseable and none do so. Return null if OC_comments is missing, empty or unparseable."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 63,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_oc_comment_introduces_verifiable_external_fact",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments) read against OP title/argument: 1 if any comment explicitly states at least one verifiable external fact not already in the OP's title/argument, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read OC_comments (JSON list of comments by users other than the OP) jointly with title and argument. Return 1 if at least one comment explicitly asserts a concrete, checkable factual claim about the external world (e.g., statistic, historical event, study finding, law, documented example, named source) that is distinct from, and not merely restating, facts or claims already in the OP's title or argument. Opinions, value judgments, hypotheticals, pure logical reasoning, rephrasing of the OP's own facts, and quotes of the OP do not count. Do not use the conversation column. Truth of the fact need not be verified; it must be verifiable in principle. Return 0 if comments parse and none qualify. Return null if OC_comments is missing, empty or unparseable, or title/argument is missing. List order is not used."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
